From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdulmajeed Almarzoqi <abdulmjad01@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:01:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Leave Google Play services out of the phone build

The phone build linked three closed-source Google libraries: ML Kit text
recognition (play-services-mlkit-text-recognition), Play Core and, through
the Wear libraries, Play services Wearable. They are now gone from it:

- The Wear libraries are the watch build's alone; the phone code names no
  Wear class. Guava, which they brought, is a dependency of its own.
- OcrController recognises no text: a request finishes at once without
  text blocks, as one does when ML Kit is not ready. Image descriptions
  keep the rest of their sources.
- Play services availability is read from the GMS core package itself, an
  installed and enabled one of at least the version the client required.
- TalkBackApplication is a plain Application: the build has no downloaded
  modules for SplitCompat to load.
